=====Usage notes=====
* Before an adjective, '''{{m|fr||de}}''' is not used when the adjective and noun form a coherent {{l|en|noun phrase}}:
*: {{ux|fr|inline=1|'''de''' petits pois|small peas}}
*: {{ux|fr|inline=1|'''des''' {{l|fr|petit pois|petits pois}}|{{l|en|green pea|green peas}}}}
: In informal speech, '''{{m|fr||de}}''' is not always used over {{m|fr|des}} before adjectives.
* In negative sentences, '''{{m|fr||de}}''' often replaces the indefinite ({{m|fr|un}}, {{m|fr|une}} and {{m|fr|des}}) and partitive articles ({{m|fr|du}}, {{m|fr|de la}}, {{m|fr|des}}); it does not replace definite articles (''Je ne comprends pas '''la'''  question.''), nor is it used when the object has no article (''Je n'ai plus faim.''). However, there are situations where the indefinite or partitive articles are retained. For example<ref>[https://bdl.oqlf.gouv.qc.ca/bdl/gabarit_bdl.asp?Th=2&t1=&id=3514 Banque de dépannage linguistique]</ref>:
** when the nominal element is an attributive complement to the negated verb {{m|fr|être}}
**: {{ux|inline=1|fr|Il n'est pas un menteur.|He isn't a liar.}}
** when the complement of the negated verb is followed by a contradistinctive element (not X, but Y)
**: {{ux|inline=1|fr|Il ne mange pas de viande.|He doesn't eat meat.}}
**: {{ux|inline=1|fr|Il ne mange pas de la viande, mais du pain.|He doesn't eat meat, but bread.}}
* The pronoun {{m|fr|en}} can replace an object introduced by {{m|fr|de}}.

