{{PIE word|nb|só}}
{{inh+|nb|gmq-mno|-}} ''the'', also ''their'',<ref>[https://www.dokpro.uio.no/cgi-bin/middelalder/diplom_vise_tekst.cgi?b=4298&s=n&str= ''Diplomatarium Norvegicum'', volume IV, no. 827], 7 May 1425, pages 602–603.</ref> from {{inh|nb|non|þeir|t=they; those}}, the nominative masculine plural of {{m|non|sá|t=that}}, from {{inh|nb|gem-pro|*þai}}, from {{inh|nb|ine-pro|*tóy}}, the nominative masculine plural of {{m|ine-pro|*só}}. The masculine plural form was generalized to all genders.

The singular gender-neutral sense is a {{semantic loan|nb|en|they|nocap=1}}.<ref name="singular-de">[https://kjonnsforskning.no/nb/2025/10/kjonnsnoytrale-pronomen-personlig-og-politisk “Kjønnsnøytrale pronomen: personlig og politisk”], in ''Kilden'', 31 October 2025, quoting Språkrådet.</ref>

Cognate with {{cog|nn|dei}}, {{cog|da|de}}, {{cog|sv|de}}, {{cog|is|þeir}}, {{cog|fo|teir}} and {{cog|de|die|t=those}}. Compare {{cog|en|they}}, borrowed from Old Norse.

