=====Usage notes=====
* {{m|nb|de|De}} is plural; the corresponding singular forms are masculine and feminine {{m|nb|den|t=that}} and neuter {{m|nb|det|t=that}}. The following noun normally takes its definite form: ''de husene'' ("those houses").
* {{m|nb|disse|Disse|t=these}} normally indicates nearer referents. Colloquial ''de her'' and ''de der'' can occur before or around a noun: ''de her husene'', ''de husene her'' ("these houses").

