=====Usage notes=====
* {{m|nb|de|De}} normally marks the subject; {{m|nb|dem|t=them}} marks an object or follows a preposition. Word order does not change this distinction.
* Before a relative clause, {{m|nb|de}} may also occur in object position or after a preposition: ''Jeg hjelper de som trenger det'' ("I help those who need it"). {{w|Language Council of Norway|Språkrådet}} recommends {{m|nb|dem}} in these positions. The same applies when ''som'' is omitted.
* Both {{m|nb|de}} and {{m|nb|dem}} occur after copular verbs and in comparisons: ''Det var de/dem'' ("It was them"), ''eldre enn de/dem'' ("older than them"). Both are also possible in cleft and existential constructions: ''Det var de/dem jeg møtte'' ("It was them I met"), ''Det finnes de/dem som mener noe annet'' ("There are those who think otherwise").
* The reflexive pronoun is {{m|nb|seg}}: ''De vasker seg'' ("They wash themselves").
* Singular gender-neutral use is found in contemporary writing but is not part of the official Bokmål norm.<ref name="singular-de"/> For formal second-person address, see {{m|nb|De|t=you}}.

